  "Id": 2196,
  "Title": "Coronavirus precautions: changes in Karachi",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Classes suspended and student hostels closed, all other activities to proceed as normal.",
  "GlobalNews": true,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>The Aga Khan University in Karachi is transitioning to an online academic environment and is adjusting teaching schedules to ensure the health and safety of students as part of the public health response to the coronavirus.<br/></p><p>All classes at the Stadium Road and Karimabad campuses in Karachi have been suspended and student hostels will be closed in the coming days. The decision follows advice by the federal government to temporarily halt academic activities at all universities and degree-awarding institutions in Pakistan, including AKU. All other business activities at the University and its teaching hospital in Karachi are to proceed as normal.<br/><br/></p><p><br/></p>",
